Tomás,

Thank you for the call last Thursday with Leo. I have discussed it with our plant managers and we would like to move to a scoped pilot rather than a broader discussion. Before Leo sends the proposal, three things I need to be clear on:

1. Implementation time. You said "four to six weeks to first forecast" for one plant. Does that assume our historian is already exporting, or does it include the connector work? Our Petaluma plant runs Ignition; the other two are on an older Wonderware setup.
2. References. I would like to speak with one customer who runs a perishable line, not metals. Northstar was mentioned; is that possible, and who would arrange it?
3. Our legal team will send our standard mutual NDA this week, before any plant data leaves our network. Please tell me who should receive it.

If the answers are what I hope, we would aim to start in early April on one plant, six weeks, with a clear go/no-go at the end. I have copied Avery, as you suggested.

